diff --git a/exachem/cc/scripts/hamiltonian_extractor/README.md b/exachem/cc/scripts/hamiltonian_extractor/README.md
index 07233be..5068b02 100644
--- a/exachem/cc/scripts/hamiltonian_extractor/README.md
+++ b/exachem/cc/scripts/hamiltonian_extractor/README.md
@@ -3 +3,4 @@
-A modular utility for extracting Hamiltonian data from ExaChem calculation output files and converting it to various formats for quantum chemistry and quantum computing applications.
+Turns a DUCC calculation's output files into a plain active-space Hamiltonian
+(one- and two-electron integrals over a fixed, orthonormal orbital set, plus
+a core/nuclear repulsion energy) and writes that Hamiltonian out in formats
+used by other tools, and/or runs a correlated calculation on it directly.
@@ -5 +8 @@ A modular utility for extracting Hamiltonian data from ExaChem calculation outpu
-## Overview
+Currently supports **closed-shell (RHF-derived) Hamiltonians only.**
@@ -7,5 +10 @@ A modular utility for extracting Hamiltonian data from ExaChem calculation outpu
-This utility processes calculation results and generates Hamiltonian representations in multiple formats:
-- **FCIDUMP**: Modified for DMRG calculations with MolMPS program
-- **YAML**: Based on Broombridge version 0.3 schema
-- **XACC**: For quantum computing applications with XACC software
-- **Info**: Human-readable analysis file
+## Input files
@@ -13 +12 @@ This utility processes calculation results and generates Hamiltonian representat
-## Requirements
+Two files, both produced by a DUCC run:
@@ -15,4 +14,7 @@ This utility processes calculation results and generates Hamiltonian representat
-- Python 3.6+
-- NumPy
-- PyYAML or ruamel.yaml (for YAML format output)
-- PySCF (for FCI calculations)
+1. **`output_file`** - the run's stdout/log. Supplies the geometry, nuclear
+   repulsion energy, active-space orbital counts (`n_occ_alpha`, `n_occ_beta`,
+   `n_virt_alpha`, `n_virt_beta`), and the DUCC energy shift.
+2. **`integral_path`** - the `<prefix>.ducc.results.txt` file. Supplies the
+   one- and two-electron integrals over the active space as a sequence of
+   `Begin <BLOCK> Block ... End` sections (`IJ`, `IA`, `AB`, `IJKL`, `ABCD`,
+   `IJAB`, `AIJB`, `IJKA`, `IABC`).
@@ -20 +22 @@ This utility processes calculation results and generates Hamiltonian representat
-## Installation
+The [`Test/`](Test/) directory has a worked H2O/6-31G example (see below).
@@ -22 +24 @@ This utility processes calculation results and generates Hamiltonian representat
-No installation required. Simply use the script directly from the `hamiltonian_extractor` directory.
+## Basic invocation
@@ -24 +26,3 @@ No installation required. Simply use the script directly from the `hamiltonian_e
-## Usage
+```bash
+python extract_hamiltonian.py <output_file> <integral_path> [options]
+```
@@ -26 +30,3 @@ No installation required. Simply use the script directly from the `hamiltonian_e
-### Basic Usage
+By default this extracts the Hamiltonian, writes `<prefix>-info`, and writes
