+### PySCF-compatible integrals (`--format pyscf`, requires PySCF)
+
+`<prefix>.pyscf.fcidump` - a **standard** FCIDUMP file, written with
+`pyscf.tools.fcidump.from_integrals`. Anyone already using PySCF can read it
+back exactly as they would any other FCIDUMP:
+
+```python
+from pyscf.tools import fcidump
+result = fcidump.read("h2o.pyscf.fcidump")
+h1e, h2e, ecore = result["H1"], result["H2"], result["ECORE"]
+```
