-   - Nuclear repulsion energy
-   - Energy shifts
-   - Orbital counts
-   - SCF and core energies
-   - Orbital energies after downfolding
+This is the recommended substitute for PySCF's own integral-generation step
+(`mol.intor(...)` / `mf.get_hcore()` / `ao2mo.kernel(...)`) when what you
+actually want are DUCC's downfolded active-space integrals: run this script
+instead of building an AO Hamiltonian yourself, and treat `h1e`/`h2e`/`ecore`
+as if they had come from PySCF directly (`h1e` and `h2e` are already in the
+active-space MO basis, in chemist notation, so no further transformation is
+needed).
