+carrying these same integrals (`mf.get_hcore()`, `mf._eri`, `mf.mo_coeff`,
+`mf.e_tot`, ...) that can be handed directly to any PySCF post-mean-field
+method, e.g. `cc.RCCSD(mf).run()` or `mp.MP2(mf).run()` - this is exactly
+what `--pyscf-ccsd` below does internally.
